# rhwp layout fixes for why-hwp, measured against Hangul 2024 output.
# Base: rhwp 7213ed1f9 after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero).
#
# - text_measurement.rs, font_metrics_technical_symbols.rs, font_metrics_data.rs:
#   HCR Batang box-drawing characters advance 970/1000 em; bold text measures
#   symbols with the regular face's advance unless the glyph is known missing.
# - picture_footnote.rs: table and picture captions draw their bullet.
# - typeset.rs: the first line of an hwpx column keeps its stored spacing-before.
# - rendering.rs: text output puts a space after a list bullet.
# - pdf.rs: PDF font fallback tries the SVG font-family list before database order.
# - font_metrics_data.rs: "한컴 윤고딕 250" uses the Haan YGodic 250 widths.
# - glyph_fit.rs: glyphs under negative letter spacing keep their own width.
# - list_marker_geometry.rs: an ASCII bullet takes a half-em cell.
# - punctuation_slots.rs: a space after Latin text advances with the Hangul em and ratio.
# - equation/: arrows use the equation font; HYhwpEQ equations keep a thin space after a function name.
# - composer/tests.rs, layout/tests.rs and the test modules above cover these changes.

